      "message": "Consider replacing the preprocessor macros for the VID/PID with `constexpr` variables inside the `ElanApp` namespace. \n\n```cpp\n// Current:\n#define BOOT_VID 0x04F3\n#define BOOT_PID 0x0910\n\n// Suggested:\nnamespace ElanApp\n{\n\tconstexpr uint16_t kBootVid \u003d 0x04F3;\n\tconstexpr uint16_t kBootPid \u003d 0x0910;\n```\n\n**Reasoning:**\nSince we are using C++23, `constexpr` is highly preferred over `#define` for constants. It provides strict type safety (`uint16_t` matches exactly what `initialize()` and `connectDevice()` expect), prevents polluting the global namespace, and retains symbols for easier debugging. This also keeps the constant management perfectly consistent with the excellent use of `constexpr` you already have for internal constants in `iapcontrol.cc`. Make sure to update the references in `iaptool.cc` to `ElanApp::kBootVid` and `ElanApp::kBootPid` as well.",
