      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Upgrade `logInfo` to `std::print`**\n\nIn `util/elan/utility.h`, you are manually combining `std::cout` with `std::format`:\n\n```c\ntemplate \u003ctypename... Args\u003e\nvoid logInfo(std::format_string\u003cArgs...\u003e fmt, Args \u0026\u0026...args)\n{\n\tstd::cout \u003c\u003c std::format(fmt, std::forward\u003cArgs\u003e(args)...);\n}\n```\n\nC++23 introduced `\u003cprint\u003e`. You can directly use `std::print` (or `std::println`), which is inherently safer, faster, and avoids the overhead of intermediate string allocation:\n\n```c\n#include \u003cprint\u003e\n#include \u003cutility\u003e // Don\u0027t forget this for std::forward!\n\ntemplate \u003ctypename... Args\u003e\nvoid logInfo(std::format_string\u003cArgs...\u003e fmt, Args \u0026\u0026...args)\n{\n\tstd::print(fmt, std::forward\u003cArgs\u003e(args)...);\n}\n```",
